From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Belo <gustavo@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 284/284] ffx_fsr2_api_x64: Implement FSR2-to-FSR4 upscale translation

Adds a new builtin dll, ffx_fsr2_api_x64.dll, that implements the AMD
FidelityFX Super Resolution 2 "context" convenience API
(ffxFsr2ContextCreate/Dispatch/Destroy and friends) and drives FSR4
upscaling under the hood, using the same "external provider" mechanism
that dlls/amdxc64 already uses to upgrade FSR 3.1 games to FSR4.

Games that dynamically load ffx_fsr2_api_x64.dll from their own install
directory (confirmed via reverse engineering the frontend/backend split
of Red Dead Redemption 2's FSR2 integration: the frontend only exports
the context API and internally loads a DX12/VK backend dll to do so)
can be redirected to this builtin with
WINEDLLOVERRIDES=ffx_fsr2_api_x64=b, without needing any game-side
binary patching. The game's own ffx_fsr2_api_dx12_x64.dll /
ffx_fsr2_api_vk_x64.dll backends are left on disk but unused in this
configuration; only the DX12 path is implemented.

The context/dispatch descriptor translation (FfxFsr2ContextDescription
-> ffxCreateContextDescUpscale, FfxFsr2DispatchDescription ->
ffxDispatchDescUpscale) follows the public FidelityFX SDK "upscale"
effect ABI (Kits/FidelityFX/upscalers/include/ffx_upscale.h) and the
FSR2 SDK's own public structures (ffx_fsr2.h / ffx_types.h), both MIT
licensed. FfxResource -> FfxApiResource field/enum translation accounts
for the differing resource type/state enumerations between the two
SDKs (confirmed by reading both headers side by side). The
ffxExternalProvider contract (structVersion, descType effect mask,
unk_data chain) was confirmed by disassembling amdxcffx64.dll's
UpdateFfxApiProviderEx export.

Gated behind PROTON_FSR2_UPGRADE=1 (see accompanying protonfixes and
proton script changes), and behind an in-dll FP8/WMMA hardware check
via wine's own amdxc64.dll (reused rather than duplicated) so it is a
no-op on unsupported hardware.

Known limitations / follow-ups for review:
 - Only tested against Red Dead Redemption 2 (DX12) on RDNA4 so far.
 - viewSpaceToMetersFactor is defensively range-clamped since its
   presence/offset in FfxFsr2DispatchDescription varies across FSR2
   2.x point releases; older games may need this revisited.
 - Motion vector scale/jitter conventions are passed through unchanged;
   FSR2 and FSR3.1/4 are believed compatible here but this is the area
   most likely to need tuning if ghosting/artifacts are observed.
